-- Adversarial: a module that shadows the prelude `Files` with its own and still needs the host
-- one imports it from `std.host`, the module spec/14 §3 says declares it.
-- Expected: accepted, or a defined rejection. spec/14 §3 says the host capabilities "are
-- declared in the module `std.host`"; spec/10 §11 rule 4 makes U1001 an import of "a module
-- of neither the package nor `std`"; rule 1 lists `std.testing` as the only module path of the
-- standard library.
-- Observed: U1001 "module `std.host` is not a module of this package or of the standard
-- library" (exit 1). The message contradicts spec/14 §3, and a module that declares or imports
-- another `Files` has no way to name the host one (finding RV2-2).
-- Verdict: Minor
module t

import std.host (Files)

pub f() -> Int = 1
